# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.

# --- Supabase -------------------------------------------------------------
# Project Settings -> Data API (URL) and API Keys (publishable key).
#
# Use the PUBLISHABLE key (sb_publishable_...). It replaces what used to be
# called the anon key and carries the same low privileges, so row-level
# security behaves identically. Legacy anon keys still work; Supabase is
# retiring them.
#
# NEVER use the SECRET key (sb_secret_..., formerly service_role) here. It
# bypasses row-level security entirely, which would show every user everyone
# else's shifts. The app refuses to start if it finds one.
#
# There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: every Supabase call in this app happens on
# the server, so neither value reaches the browser. On Vercel these are
# ordinary (private) environment variables — no "expose to the browser" prompt.
#
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and the NEXT_PUBLIC_ names also work, as fallbacks.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# --- Anthropic ------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that would ship the
# key to every browser that loads the app.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- Supabase dashboard setup (not env vars, but required) ----------------
# Sign-in uses a numeric code rather than a magic link, so the session is
# created inside the installed PWA instead of in Safari.
#
# FIRST: custom SMTP must be enabled, under Authentication -> Emails -> SMTP
# Settings. Since June 2026 new free-tier projects on Supabase's built-in email
# provider cannot edit templates, and that provider only delivers to addresses
# on the project's team at 2 messages/hour — so it cannot serve real users
# either way. Gmail works with an app password and needs no domain.
#
# THEN: two templates must be changed, under Authentication -> Emails:
#
#   - "Confirm signup"  — sent on a user's FIRST ever sign-in, when the account
#                         is created. Easy to miss; it is not the Magic Link one.
#   - "Magic Link"      — sent on every sign-in after that.
#
# In both, replace the {{ .ConfirmationURL }} anchor with:
#
#     <p>Your Cash Out sign-in code is: <strong>{{ .Token }}</strong></p>
#
# Editing only Magic Link means the very first sign-in still receives a link,
# which opens in Safari and lands the session outside the installed PWA.
